 journal of what I was doing and a day-in  day-out and tried to think about the the  moments in my professional career that  got me really excited where I got a lot  of hi and from there you know you can  try to design a business around it so  ideally as an entrepreneur you can  structure the company however you want  to structure the company and you want to  make it around something that gives you  a lot of excitement and enjoyment so I  found that creating that journal really  helped me for that period of  in my life were I was able to record  what I really like doing and what I  didn't really like doing so much and  around what I really enjoyed doing was  helping entrepreneurs connecting with  entrepreneurs meeting people you know  knowing that I was able to help their  businesses and from there I was able to  build a new business out of that so  hopefully that helps you the other thing  that I found was you don't have to  commit to something right away so after  I sold my business I didn't know what I  was gonna do next I you know was looking  at a couple of opportunities what I was  interested in at the time was raising  capital because you know we hadn't  really done it for our business  everything was bootstrap from the  beginning but I was interested in the  process of raising capital so I  connected with the venture capital  company in my city and started helping  them raise capital for entrepreneurs and  learning about that process and that was  something that was interesting for me I  didn't know if it was gonna be a new  career choice or a new business it was  just something that was interesting so I  was just following one of my potential  passions and I was curious to learn more  about it and that led me to eventually  starting Evan chimerical com where are  the sharing resources and information  and I was you know able to leave the  venture capital business after a couple  years to want to start my own business  all over again  now that happened because I wasn't  committed to you know starting a new  business right away I didn't know what I  wanted to do and the best thing to do  when you're you know trying to figure  that out  it's trial aughts of different things  and see what sticks so if you're  interested in something you think you  might be able to help people in a  certain way just start trying it and see  if you enjoy it see if you get a lot of  pleasure from it see if you are able to  help people out so you don't have to  make this huge big plan at the beginning  and a lot of people get stuck in the  planning phases and then don't actually  end up ever doing anything and you can  get stuck planning for so long you  create this fantastic plan and then you  launch your business and you don't like  what you're doing there didn't work out  the way you think it was gonna work out  and it never works out the way you think  you're gonna work out so the best way is  just start start small fail small see if  you like it if you like it a little bit  try it a little  more see if you like that more see if  you able to help people and from there  you'll you'll eventually hit something  that you really enjoy doing that you re  without a lot of value to people's lives  and you wanna you want to pursue more  you want to make it your life's mission  you want to start a business around it  and continue to move forward with it so  don't be afraid of starting small and  trying something that you're kind of  interested in but you don't have to  commit yourself to doing go once try it  see if you like it or not and kind of  build from there and eventually start  hitting on points that you find are  really interesting for you and you're  able to help a lot of people with so  hopefully that helps for those watching  I'd love to hear we have to think I love  to hear you found your passion and how  you started your business if you want to  leave a comment under the video or if  you have a question that's why I can  leave it in t